{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/real-analysis-measure/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"real-number-system-completeness","title":"实数系与完备性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/real-analysis-measure/foundations/real-number-system-completeness","wordCount":1736,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"sequences-limits-rigor","title":"序列与极限的严格化（ε-N）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/real-analysis-measure/foundations/sequences-limits-rigor","wordCount":1473,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"metric-topology-basics","title":"度量与拓扑基础（开闭集与紧致性）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/real-analysis-measure/foundations/metric-topology-basics","wordCount":1478,"readingTime":6}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础\">基础</h1><p>有理数已经稠密得让人挑不出毛病：任意两个有理数之间都还塞得下无穷多个有理数。可就是这样一个「看不出窟窿」的数系，连 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.04em;vertical-align:-0.1328em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9072em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:0.833em;\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.8672em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:0.853em;height:1.08em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.08em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1080\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M95,702\nc-2.7,0,-7.17,-2.7,-13.5,-8c-5.8,-5.3,-9.5,-10,-9.5,-14\nc0,-2,0.3,-3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1328em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 都装不下，一列明明越挤越近的有理数也可能没有有理数极限。实分析的第一件事，就是诊断出这个窟窿，并用「完备性」把它补上——这是整个学科得以站立的那块基石。</p>\n<p>本章三篇文档按依赖顺序排列。第一篇讲实数系与完备性，把确界存在、单调有界收敛、柯西收敛、闭区间套这几个等价命题讲透，说明它们为什么是同一件事的不同说法。第二篇把极限本身严格化，用 ε-N 语言重新定义数列收敛，证明极限的四则运算与夹逼，引入上下极限和子列，并用 Bolzano-Weierstrass 定理把完备性兑现成具体的收敛工具。第三篇把视野从实数轴抬高到一般度量空间，定义开集、闭集、邻域与紧致性，给出实数上的 Heine-Borel 定理，为后面连续、积分、<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 空间提供统一的拓扑语言。</p>\n<p>这三篇是全 hub 的公共词汇表。后面所有章节——连续性、微分、黎曼与勒贝格积分、泛函基础——都默认你已经能熟练使用确界、极限和紧致性。如果只读一章，也请把这一章读完整：地基不牢，上面盖什么都会塌。读完基础，自然过渡到<a href=\"../continuity-differentiation/\">连续与微分</a>。</p>\n"}